  en: {
    back: '← ~/products',
    tag: 'HARDWARE',
    name: 'SPU — Swarm Processing Unit',
    tagline: 'On-board swarm autonomy that bolts onto any existing UAV — every unit plans for itself and keeps flying the mission when the operator link is gone.',
    body: "Most swarm products either replace your flight stack or route every coordination decision through a ground station and a live link. The SPU does neither. It rides alongside your existing autopilot as a companion module, and every unit plans and decides for itself, on-board — off shared state every unit keeps in step with its neighbours, with a goal-directed planner running identically on every one. There is no operator in the decision loop and no central coordinator to lose. Cut the link to the operator and the swarm keeps flying the mission; lose half the fleet and the rest keeps coordinating. That's not a fallback mode — it's the only mode there is.",
    videoLabel: 'The SPU in under five minutes',
    videoCaption: "What it is, Loom and the Mission Studio, the ground station, then recorded scenario runs replayed in its tactical map. In the flight footage, positions, goals and claims are recorded; the camera, trails and markers are staged; synthetic flight model where noted.",
    specsTitle: 'Specifications',
    specs: [
      "Zephyr RTOS firmware, one image — drone or ground-control role set at configuration time",
      "Decentralized coordination runtime (fleece): replicated shared state plus goal-oriented mission planning, running on every unit",
      "Its own mesh over any transparent serial radio — no internet, no cloud, no single point of failure; every frame sealed with XChaCha20-Poly1305 under a provisioned fleet key",
